Version 2.62.3

librsvg-2.0 C library for rendering SVG to Cairo 
The public name, soname, and pkg-config module remain librsvg-2.0.
Build with the usual ./configure && make. Install with make install.
Use DESTDIR when packaging or when you do not want to replace 
the system librsvg-2.0. Development used automated assistance. 
All commits are reviewed and owned by the maintainer. 
This is not an official GNOME release.

Stylesheet engine
- libcroco is discontinued: not compiled, not linked, not packaged.
  `libcroco/` stays in the tree as an unbuilt 0.6.15 archive. css/
  is the only stylesheet engine. `RSVG_CSS_ENGINE` is ignored
  (`RSVG_CSS_ENGINE=croco` included).  CSS cascade walk depth is
  capped.  A stray `}` in a stylesheet no longer stalls the css/
  parser.

Public API
- Public API includes render_document / render_layer /
  render_element, geometry queries, intrinsic size,
  set_stylesheet, context-fill / context-stroke, and
  rsvg_handle_set_cancellable_for_rendering (cancel returns
  G_IO_ERROR / G_IO_ERROR_CANCELLED).

SVG <image> rasters
- SVG <image> decodes PNG (libpng), JPEG (libjpeg /
  libjpeg-turbo), GIF (giflib), WebP (libwebp), and BMP
  (in-tree decoder).  Optional AVIF uses libavif (configure
  --enable-avif, default auto).  --disable-bmp omits BMP;
  --enable-bmp needs no extra library.  --disable-* omits a
  decoder; --enable-* without the library is an error for
  PNG/JPEG/GIF/WebP/AVIF.  Known rasters do not fall through
  to gdk-pixbuf.
- GIF <image> uses the first frame, GCE transparency, local then
  global palette, and interlaced frames.  BMP <image> uses
  Windows DIB (uncompressed 1/4/8/24/32-bit and common RLE).
  SVG <image> rejects oversized rasters (dimension and pixel
  caps) before decode; BMP RLE stays inside the destination
  buffer.

Defaults
- Default handle DPI is 96.  rsvg-convert also
  defaults to 96dpi; use -d 90 -p 90 for the previous CLI default.

rsvg-convert (GLib GOption; not clap)
- User CLI is rsvg-convert only.  Help is not identical to GNOME
  2.62.3 (clap).  This tree has --stylesheet / -s (reads a CSS
  file and calls rsvg_handle_set_stylesheet) and stdin as no
  filename or as "-".  `-f pdf1.4` … `pdf1.7` call
  cairo_pdf_surface_restrict_to_version; plain `-f pdf` is
  unrestricted (same as before).  Formats xml and recording are
  kept.
- `--page-width` / `--page-height` set output media size (default =
  rendered image size).  `--left` / `--top` offset the image from
  the page origin (default 0).  Pixel numbers only (optional `px`);
  CSS lengths (mm, in, …) are not parsed.  Units match this
  convert’s `-w`/`-h` (PNG pixels; PDF/PS/EPS cairo user units —
  not rust’s px→pt conversion, so default PDF size is unchanged).
  Image + offset larger than the page is clipped; the page does
  not grow.  Applies to PNG, PDF/PS/EPS, and SVG, as in rust 2.62.
- `-w` / `--width` and `-h` / `--height` accept CSS lengths:
  bare numbers keep today’s meaning (PNG pixels; PDF/PS cairo
  user units).  With a unit (`px`, `pt`, `pc`, `in`, `cm`, `mm`)
  values resolve like rust 2.62 for that format (PNG: CSS px at
  DPI; PDF/PS/EPS: points, including px→pt).  `em` / `ex` / `%`
  are rejected.  `--page-*` / `--left` / `--top` stay pixel
  numbers.
- `-l` / `--accept-language` is a comma-separated BCP47 list
  (`es-MX,de,en`, optional `q=` weights).  Invalid tags fail with
  stderr and exit 1 (same as rust).  When set, `systemLanguage` /
  `<switch>` matching uses that list instead of `LANG`.  No flag:
  host locale unchanged.  Does not change process locale; the same
  list applies to every file in a multi-file run.
- Bash Tab completion is a static file shipped in librsvg-c-bin
  at `/usr/share/bash-completion/completions/rsvg-convert`.
  rsvg-convert has no `--completion` flag (clap-only; permanently
  out of scope).
- `--version` and `--help` print a short GNU GPL-2.0-only notice
  (not the full LICENCE file), with
  `Copyright (C) 1999-2026 The librsvg C library authors`
  (same span as `doc/copyright.md`).  Verified against this tree:
  LICENCE is GNU GPL Version 2, June 1991; COPYING maps
  rsvg-convert to “GNU General Public License, version 2” with
  no “or later”, so the notice is GPL-2.0-only (not
  GPL-2.0-or-later).  LICENCE-LIB is GNU Library GPL v2 or later
  and applies to librsvg-2.so / headers only — those strings are
  unchanged.  rsvg.h and rsvg-base.c still say Library GPL v2 or
  later.  TTY stdin still prints the same short GPL-2 notice plus
  “Reading from standard input” / Control-C; pipes stay quiet.

CSS / paint
- CSS: selectors and specificity; Color Level 4; font-size
  smaller / larger; paint-order; mix-blend-mode; isolation;
  mask-type; vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke.

Filters
- Filters: feDropShadow, CSS filter() functions, feColorMatrix
  hueRotate in degrees, feConvolveMatrix, lighting, component
  transfer.

Text / geometry
- Text objectBoundingBox paint uses the union of text-span
  ink boxes.  Radial gradients accept fr (focal radius).

URL / security limits
- SVG2 href (wins over xlink:href).  File URL loads reject
  http(s)/ftp, file://hostname/, query strings, and fragments.
  Encoded data: URIs over 64 MiB are rejected before decode.
  CSS number lists (tableValues, dasharray) are capped at 4096
  tokens.

gdk-pixbuf loader
- The gdk-pixbuf SVG loader keeps the first GError, frees its
  context if load_increment never ran, honors rsvg_handle_close,
  and uses rsvg_handle_get_pixbuf_and_error.

Build
- libxml2 2.15: include parser.h (not SAX.h) for xmlParserCtxtPtr.
  When xmlParserMaxDepth is a writable global, raise it to the CSS
  walk bound (no XML_PARSE_HUGE).  When it is a non-assignable macro
  (256), parse options include XML_PARSE_HUGE so deep CSS trees
  parse.  xml-stylesheet pseudo-attributes use xmlReadMemory
  (length is strlen, no extra NUL).  rsvg-convert uses
  rsvg_handle_set_dpi_x_y, get_geometry_for_element /
  get_intrinsic_size_in_pixels, and render_document /
  render_element instead of the deprecated viewport helpers.
- Deprecated public symbols remain exported (2.62.3 ABI).  Current
  APIs no longer call those names for document size, pixbuf render,
  or in-memory load; they share internal helpers.  Do not treat the
  ABI as deprecation-free.
- Debian/Devuan packages (`librsvg-c2` and friends) replace
  `librsvg2-*`.  Install all needed local debs in one `apt-get
  install ./….deb` command (`deb/INSTALL.md`).  `librsvg-c-dev`
  Depends on the `-dev` packages named in `librsvg-2.0.pc`
  (including libxml2, gif, avif).  Runtime `librsvg-c2` Depends on
  libgif7.  `deb/install.sh` runtime set is c2+common+bin; `-dev`
  is optional (missing `-dev` is not a checksum or install error).
  `install.sh --verify-gpg` is opt-in (default stays sha256sum + apt).
  dpkg “removing anyway” lines during the GNOME librsvg2-* replace
  are expected (`deb/INSTALL.md`).

Version 2.59.0 (Not released)
- rsvg_handle_set_cancellable_for_rendering().  Cancelling a
  render returns G_IO_ERROR / G_IO_ERROR_CANCELLED.
- CSS cascade: selectors, specificity, UA / User / Author
  origins.
- data: URLs with an empty MIME and ;base64 decode; negative
  rect rx/ry ignored; negative stroke-dashoffset honored;
  square linecaps on zero-length subpaths.
- Path S/T keep separate cubic and quadratic reflection
  points.  Marker orientation when Bézier controls coincide.
  feColorMatrix hueRotate is in degrees.
- Pattern fills use the path object bounding box.
  fill-opacity applies to pattern tiles.
- Radial gradients accept SVG2 fr (default 0).
- Referenced file URLs reject query strings and fragments.
  http(s)/ftp and file://hostname/ remain denied.
- SVG <image> decodes WebP with libwebp (MIME image/webp,
  RIFF/WEBP sniff, or .webp href).  --disable-webp omits it.

Version 2.52.0 (Not released)
- Public name, soname, and pkg-config remain librsvg-2.0.
- New public APIs: rsvg_handle_render_document,
  rsvg_handle_render_layer, rsvg_handle_render_element,
  rsvg_handle_get_geometry_for_layer,
  rsvg_handle_get_geometry_for_element,
  rsvg_handle_get_intrinsic_dimensions,
  rsvg_handle_get_intrinsic_size_in_pixels,
  rsvg_handle_get_pixbuf_and_error, rsvg_handle_set_stylesheet.
  fill/stroke accept context-fill and context-stroke.
- SVG2 href in addition to xlink:href (href wins if both are
  set) on use, image, pattern, gradients, tref, and filter
  image.
- paint-order (fill / stroke / markers).
- mix-blend-mode and isolation.
- mask-type: luminance (default) or alpha.
- vector-effect: non-scaling-stroke on paths.
- Referenced-file loads reject http(s)/ftp and
  file://hostname/; relative file paths must stay under the
  document’s directory.


Version 2.40.21
- CVE-2019-20446 - Backport the following fixes from 2.46.x:

- #515 - Librsvg now has limits on the number of loaded XML elements,
  and the number of referenced elements within an SVG document.  This
  is to mitigate malicious SVGs which try to consume all memory, and
  those which try to consume an exponential amount of CPU time.

- #308 - Fix stack exhaustion with circular references in <use> elements.

- #323 - Fix a denial-of-service condition from exponential explosion
  of rendered elements, through nested use of SVG "use" elements in
  malicious SVGs.  This is similar to the XML "billion laughs attack"
  but for SVG instancing.

Version 2.40.20
- Except for emergencies, this will be the LAST RELEASE of the
  librsvg-2.40.x series.  We are moving to 2.41, which is vastly
  improved over the 2.40 series.  The API/ABI there remain unchaged,
  so we strongly encourage you to upgrade your sources and binaries to
  librsvg-2.41.x.
- bgo#761175 - Allow masks and clips to reuse a node being drawn.
- Don't access the file system when deciding whether to load a remote
  file with a UNC path for a paint server (i.e. don't try to load it at all).
- Vistual Studio: fixed and integrated introspection builds, so
  introspection data is built directly from the Visual Studio project
  (Chun-wei Fan).
- Visual Studio: We now use HIGHENTROPYVA linker option on x64 builds,
  to enhance the security of built binaries (Chun-wei Fan).
- Fix generation of Vala bindings when compiling in read-only source
  directories (Emmanuele Bassi).

Version 2.40.19
- bgo#621088: Using text objects as clipping paths is now supported.
- bgo#587721: Fix rendering of text elements with transformations (Massimo).
- bgo#777833 - Fix memory leaks when an RsvgHandle is disposed before
  being closed (Philip Withnall).
- bgo#782098 - Don't pass deprecated options to gtk-doc (Ting-Wei Lan).
- bgo#786372 - Fix the default for the "type" attribute of the <style> element.
- bgo#785276 - Don't crash on single-byte files.
- bgo#634514: Don't render unknown elements and their sub-elements.
- bgo#777155 - Ignore patterns that have close-to-zero dimensions.
- bgo#634324 - Fix Gaussian blurs with negative scaling.
- Fix the <switch> element; it wasn't working at all.
- Fix loading when rsvg_handle_write() is called one byte at a time.
- bgo#787895 - Fix incorrect usage of libxml2.  Thanks to Nick Wellnhofer
  for advice on this.
- Backported the test suite machinery from the master branch (Chun-wei Fan,
  Federico Mena).
- We now require Pango 1.38.0 or later (released in 2015).
- We now require libxml2 2.9.0 or later (released in 2012).

Version 2.40.18
- bgo#783835 - CVE-2017-11464 - Fix division-by-zero in the Gaussian
  blur code.
- Fix other cases of division-by-zero on fuzzed SVG files.
- Don't crash on invalid transformation matrices.
- Support Visual Studio 2017; generate .pc files for Meson on Windows -
  Chun-wei Fan.

Version 2.40.17
- bgo#778666 - Use our own thumbnailer specification file, so
  gnome-desktop-thumbnailer can generate thumbnails outside of the
  calling process (Jeremy Bicha).
- Removed some redundant code.
- Windows build fixes - Chun-wei Fan.

Version 2.40.16
- Chun-wei Fan added support for building the introspection files under MSVC.
- Fixed bgo#760262 - Make the zooming options in rsvg-convert(1) work again
  for scaling the resulting image.  Fix by Menner <mix@gmx.org>.
- Fixed bgo#764808 - Wikipedia generates equations as SVGs and renders
  them, but uses fill="currentColor".  Since we don't let callers
  specify a starting state for CSS, we need to start with opaque black
  as the default current color.
- Added documentation for how to replace the deprecated
  rsvg_handle_set_size_callback().

Version 2.40.15
- Apologies for the lack of 2.40.14.  I mistakenly tagged the
  repository before updating the NEWS file.
- librsvg now uses the Contributor Covenant Code of Conduct, 
  version 1.4, to which all contributors and maintainers are expected
  to abide. Please see the code_of_conduct.md file for details.
- Chun-wei Fan fixed builds on Visual Studio pre-2012.
- Fixed bgo#759084 - Don't crash when filters don't actually exist
  Fix by Benjamin Otte.
- Javier Jardón updated our autogen.sh to use modern autotools.
- Fixed bgo#761728 - Memory leak in the PrimitiveComponentTransfer
  filter.  Fix by Ron Hopper.

Version 2.40.13
- Chun-wei Fan and Paolo Borelli fixed the Windows build.
- Menner added basic support for the "baseline-shift" attribute in
  text objects.  We support "sub", "super", and plain "baseline", so
  you can at least have subscripts and superscripts for formulas and
  such.  There is no support for percentages or explicit lengths yet.
  bgo#340047.
- Menner fixed some duplicate logic when rendering paths, which would
  try to decide whether to create intermediate surfaces.  Now we have
  a single place where this is done.  This fixes inconsistent text
  spacing in some situations.  bgo#749415.
- Rewrote the markers engine, for bgo#685906 and bgo#760180 - Our
  machinery for rendering SVG markers (like arrowheads and such)
  didn't handle several cases correctly.  Curves with coincident
  control points produced incorrect orientations for the markers, as
  did multiple contiguous zero-length segments.  We follow the spec
  for this now and handle things correctly.  Also, markers didn't
  render in the correct position if they had the viewBox attribute
  set.

Version 2.40.12
- Benjamin Otte did *great* work in refactoring the test harness to
  use Glib's gtest infrastructure, instead of using home-grown
  machinery.  Tests can simply be put as SVG files in the tests/
  subdirectories; it is not necessary to list them explicitly in some
  text file.  Yay!
- Gzipped SVGs now work if read from streams.
- References to objects/filters/URIs/etc. are now handled lazily.
  Also, there is a general-purpose cycle detector so malformed SVGs
  don't cause infinite loops.  Work by Benjamin Otte.
- Removed parsing of Adobe blend modes; they were not implemented, anyway.
- Fixed bgo#700911 - feComponentTransfer filter functions did not work at all.
- Fixed bgo#630732 - out-of-bounds read in feComponentTransfer with tableValues.
- Fixed bgo#677068 - incorrect reflection points in paths.

Version 2.40.11
- Add project files for building on Visual Studio (bgo#753555).  Work
  by Chun-wei Fan.
- Added an "--export-id" option to rsvg-convert(1).  This lets you
  select a single object to export, for example, to pick out a group
  from a multi-part drawing.  Note that this is mostly useful for PNG
  output right now; for SVG output we don't preserve many attributes
  which could be useful in the extracted version.  Doing this properly
  requires an internal "output to SVG" backend instead of just telling
  Cairo to render to SVG.

Version 2.40.10
- Fixed bgo#748608 - Memory leak when Gaussian-blurring.  Thanks to
  Carlos Garnacho for fixing my leaky code.
- Fixed bgo#739329 - font-family attributes with singly-quoted names
  were not handled correctly, yielding incorrect fonts.  Patch by Menner.
- Fixed bgo#476507 - Path start/end markers didn't have the correct angle
  if the path was a curve with coincident control points.  Patch by Menner.
- Fixed bgo#688689 - Support font-style="normal" within a non-normal
  styled text block.  Patch by Paolo.
- Fixed builddir != srcdir.  Patch by Matthias Clasen.
- Remove a bunch of deprecated GTK+ calls.
- This version of librsvg requires GTK+ 3.10.0, which is, ahem, only two years old.
  We previously required a version of GTK+ which is four years old.  Out with
  the old, in with the old.

